{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"sdd_title","type":"text","text":"# Unified SDD Ontology\n\nA universal taxonomy encompassing all stages, capabilities, and cross-cutting concerns\nacross 6 harness frameworks: **GSD · OpenSpec · Spec Kit · Kiro · BMAD · Taskmaster AI**\n\n*Each stage and capability is annotated with which frameworks implement it and which do not.*","x":300,"y":-720,"width":700,"height":160,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"sdd_pipeline_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":-480,"width":2500,"height":2040,"color":"6","label":"Universal SDD Pipeline — 10 Stages"},
		{"id":"sdd_s1","type":"text","text":"## S1: Project Initialization\n\nBootstrap project structure, install tooling,\nconfigure AI runtime, create initial artifacts.\n\n**GSD** — `/gsd:new-project` creates PROJECT.md,\nresearchers gather domain context, generates\nREQUIREMENTS.md + ROADMAP.md in one flow\n**OpenSpec** — `openspec init` creates openspec/ dir\n**Spec Kit** — `specify init <name>` with --ai flag,\ncreates .speckit/ + scripts + templates\n**Kiro** — Click + in Specs pane, IDE handles setup\n**BMAD** — `npx bmad-method install` selects modules\n**Taskmaster** — `task-master init` creates .taskmaster/\n\n---\n✅ All 6 frameworks cover this stage","x":-580,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sdd_s2","type":"text","text":"## S2: Governing Principles\n\nEstablish project values, architectural constraints,\ncoding standards, and non-negotiable rules that\nguide all downstream AI behavior.\n\n**Spec Kit** — `constitution.md` via `/speckit.constitution`\nExplicit project principles document\n**Kiro** — Steering Rules guide AI behavior\n(code style, architecture, framework prefs)\n**GSD** — PROJECT.md carries vision (always loaded)\nbut not formalized as \"constitution\"\n\n---\n✅ Spec Kit, Kiro\n⚠️ GSD (partial — PROJECT.md serves similar role)\n❌ OpenSpec, BMAD, Taskmaster","x":-180,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"sdd_s3","type":"text","text":"## S3: Requirements / Specification\n\nCapture what to build and why — user stories,\nacceptance criteria, constraints, scope.\n\n**GSD** — REQUIREMENTS.md (scoped v1/v2 with\nphase traceability), generated during new-project\n**OpenSpec** — `proposal.md` (why + scope) +\n`specs/` directory (requirements by capability)\n**Spec Kit** — `spec.md` via `/speckit.specify`\n(what & why, not how)\n**Kiro** — `requirements.md` with user stories +\nacceptance criteria (or `bugfix.md` for bugs)\n**BMAD** — PRD created by Analyst + PM agents,\ncomprehensive requirements document\n**Taskmaster** — `prd.txt` in .taskmaster/docs/\n(natural language, parsed by AI)\n\n---\n✅ All 6 frameworks cover this stage","x":220,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sdd_s4","type":"text","text":"## S4: Human-AI Discussion / Clarification\n\nInteractive dialogue to surface ambiguities,\nresolve gray areas, align on decisions before\ncommitting to a design or plan.\n\n**GSD** — `/gsd:discuss-phase [N]` surfaces\nvisual, API, content, org decisions;\n`--auto` for non-interactive defaults\n**Spec Kit** — `/speckit.clarify` addresses\nunderspecified areas before planning\n**BMAD** — Human-in-loop at each transition\n(PRD approval, architecture sign-off,\nstory approval)\n\n---\n✅ GSD (dedicated stage)\n✅ Spec Kit (dedicated command)\n⚠️ BMAD (implicit in agent interactions)\n❌ OpenSpec, Kiro, Taskmaster","x":620,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sdd_s5","type":"text","text":"## S5: Roadmap / Milestone Planning\n\nDecompose project into ordered phases or milestones\nwith dependency tracking and completion criteria.\n\n**GSD** — ROADMAP.md with numbered phases,\nadd/insert/remove phases dynamically,\nmilestone-level lifecycle management\n(audit → complete → new-milestone)\n**BMAD** — Roadmapping stage in 6-stage lifecycle,\nstructured by Analyst + PM agents\n\n---\n✅ GSD (comprehensive)\n⚠️ BMAD (covered in planning stage)\n❌ OpenSpec, Spec Kit, Kiro, Taskmaster\n\n*Most frameworks skip project-level roadmapping\nand operate at feature/task granularity instead.*","x":1020,"y":-430,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_s6","type":"text","text":"## S6: Architecture / Technical Design\n\nDefine technical approach, component design,\nsequence diagrams, data flow, error handling.\n\n**OpenSpec** — `design.md` per change\n(technical approach, architecture decisions)\n**Spec Kit** — `plan.md` via `/speckit.plan`\n(tech stack, architecture, integration)\n**Kiro** — `design.md` with sequence diagrams,\ndata flow, testing strategy\n**BMAD** — Architect agent produces system\ndesign, tech stack, integration architecture\n**GSD** — Research agents investigate architecture\nas part of plan-phase, but no standalone\ndesign document\n\n---\n✅ OpenSpec, Spec Kit, Kiro, BMAD\n⚠️ GSD (embedded in research, not standalone)\n❌ Taskmaster","x":-580,"y":20,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sdd_s7","type":"text","text":"## S7: Task Decomposition / Planning\n\nBreak design into discrete, executable work units\nwith dependencies, ordering, and verification criteria.\n\n**GSD** — `/gsd:plan-phase` creates atomic\nXML-structured plans ({N}-{M}-PLAN.md),\nplan checker validates against requirements\n**OpenSpec** — `tasks.md` implementation checklist\n**Spec Kit** — `tasks/` directory via `/speckit.tasks`\n(small, reviewable, independently testable)\n**Kiro** — `tasks.md` with real-time status tracking\n(in-progress/completed), run individually or batch\n**BMAD** — Epic Sharding: Scrum Master decomposes\nPRD into hyper-detailed self-contained story files\nwith embedded rationale + testing criteria\n**Taskmaster** — `task-master parse-prd` auto-\ndecomposes PRD into tasks with dependencies,\nsubtask expansion on demand\n\n---\n✅ All 6 frameworks cover this stage","x":-180,"y":20,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"sdd_s8","type":"text","text":"## S8: Execution / Implementation\n\nAI agent(s) write code following the plan/tasks,\nproducing commits, handling errors, managing state.\n\n**GSD** — `/gsd:execute-phase` runs parallel waves,\nfresh 200K context per task, atomic git commits,\nstuck loop detection, crash recovery\n**OpenSpec** — `/opsx:apply` implements tasks\nfollowing specs + design\n**Spec Kit** — `/speckit.implement` executes all tasks\nrespecting constitution + spec + plan\n**Kiro** — Run tasks individually or collectively\nfrom IDE with built-in agent\n**BMAD** — Dev agent implements each story file\nwith full context embedded\n**Taskmaster** — Manual/chat-driven: \"Help me\nimplement task [N]\", `task-master move`\nfor stage transitions\n\n---\n✅ All 6 frameworks cover this stage\n\n*Execution sophistication varies widely:\nGSD (parallel waves, context isolation) vs\nTaskmaster (manual chat guidance)*","x":220,"y":20,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sdd_s9","type":"text","text":"## S9: Verification / Quality Assurance\n\nValidate that implementation meets requirements,\nrun tests, check consistency, audit quality.\n\n**GSD** — `/gsd:verify-work` (goal-backward analysis),\nVERIFICATION.md report, UAT agent,\n`/gsd:ui-review` (6-pillar visual audit)\n**OpenSpec** — `/opsx:verify` validates implementation\nagainst specs, `/opsx:sync` checks drift\n**Spec Kit** — `/speckit.analyze` (cross-artifact\nconsistency), `/speckit.checklist` (requirements\ncompleteness)\n**Kiro** — Bugfix specs include regression validation;\nfeature verification through task completion\n**BMAD** — Testing criteria embedded in story files;\nno dedicated verification agent\n\n---\n✅ GSD (comprehensive)\n✅ OpenSpec, Spec Kit (spec-level validation)\n⚠️ Kiro (partial — bugfix validation only)\n⚠️ BMAD (criteria exist, no dedicated stage)\n❌ Taskmaster","x":620,"y":20,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sdd_s10","type":"text","text":"## S10: Completion / Archive / Deploy\n\nArchive completed work, tag releases, prepare\nfor next iteration, manage lifecycle transitions.\n\n**GSD** — `/gsd:complete-milestone` archives +\ntags release, `/gsd:audit-milestone` verifies\ndefinition of done, `/gsd:new-milestone` starts\nnext cycle, `/gsd:cleanup` removes phase dirs\n**OpenSpec** — `/opsx:archive` stores completed\nchanges in `archive/` with timestamps\n**BMAD** — Deployment stage in 6-stage lifecycle\n(release management)\n\n---\n✅ GSD (comprehensive lifecycle)\n✅ OpenSpec (archive system)\n⚠️ BMAD (deployment stage exists)\n❌ Spec Kit, Kiro, Taskmaster\n\n*Most spec-focused tools consider their job\ndone after implementation.*","x":1020,"y":20,"width":380,"height":400,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":480,"width":2500,"height":500,"color":"4","label":"Cross-Cutting Capabilities"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc1","type":"text","text":"## CC1: Multi-Agent Orchestration\n\nMultiple specialized AI agents with\ndistinct roles and responsibilities.\n\n✅ **GSD** — 12+ agents (researchers,\nplanner, checker, executors, verifier,\ndebugger, UI specialists)\n✅ **BMAD** — 12+ personas (Analyst,\nPM, Architect, SM, Dev, UX Designer)\n⚠️ **Kiro** — Built-in agents but\nnot user-configurable\n❌ **OpenSpec** — No agents\n❌ **Spec Kit** — No agents\n(research agents during specify only)\n❌ **Taskmaster** — Multi-role config\nbut single agent, not multi-agent","x":-580,"y":530,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc2","type":"text","text":"## CC2: Context Engineering\n\nManaging context window limits via\nisolation, fresh contexts, or artifact-\nbased state transfer.\n\n✅ **GSD** — Fresh 200K per task,\nmodular file loading, XML prompts,\nsize limits enforced\n✅ **BMAD** — Self-contained story\nfiles (zero external context needed)\n⚠️ **Taskmaster** — Progressive tool\ndisclosure (TASK_MASTER_TOOLS:\nall/standard/core)\n⚠️ **Kiro** — IDE manages context\n❌ **OpenSpec** — No context mgmt\n❌ **Spec Kit** — No context mgmt\n\n*Context isolation is the key differentiator\nbetween execution-first and spec-first tools*","x":-180,"y":530,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc3","type":"text","text":"## CC3: Multi-Runtime / Multi-Provider\n\nSupporting multiple AI backends,\nIDEs, or coding assistants.\n\n✅ **GSD** — 6 runtimes (Claude Code,\nOpenCode, Gemini CLI, Codex,\nCopilot, Antigravity)\n✅ **Spec Kit** — 20+ agents via\nAGENT_CONFIG registry + generic\n✅ **OpenSpec** — 20+ tools\n(any markdown-reading tool)\n✅ **Taskmaster** — 10+ providers\n(Anthropic, OpenAI, Gemini, Mistral,\nGroq, Ollama, OpenRouter, xAI, Azure)\n⚠️ **BMAD** — Claude Code + Cursor\n+ generic (limited)\n❌ **Kiro** — Kiro IDE only\n(locked to Claude Sonnet via Bedrock)","x":220,"y":530,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc4","type":"text","text":"## CC4: Git Integration\n\nAtomic commits, branch management,\nrelease tagging, version control of\nartifacts alongside code.\n\n✅ **GSD** — Atomic commits per task,\nbranch management, release tags,\nmilestone lifecycle, bisectable history\n✅ **OpenSpec** — Git-native specs,\nversion-controlled living docs,\nspec deltas track evolution\n✅ **Spec Kit** — Git init, .gitattributes,\nartifacts in version control\n⚠️ **BMAD** — Not explicitly documented\n⚠️ **Kiro** — IDE-managed\n❌ **Taskmaster** — No git integration","x":620,"y":530,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc5","type":"text","text":"## CC5: Dependency Management\n\nTracking task dependencies, ordering\nexecution, preventing conflicts.\n\n✅ **GSD** — Wave-based execution:\nindependent tasks parallel,\ndependent tasks sequential,\nfile conflict detection\n✅ **Taskmaster** — Dependency\nvalidation, auto-correction,\nprevents broken dependency chains,\ncross-tag movement checks\n⚠️ **BMAD** — Story sequencing by\nScrum Master\n❌ **OpenSpec** — Not applicable\n❌ **Spec Kit** — Not applicable\n❌ **Kiro** — Task ordering only","x":1020,"y":530,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc6","type":"text","text":"## CC6: Guardrails / Back-Pressure\n\nRuntime enforcement preventing bad\noutcomes: destructive writes, secret\nexposure, force-push, etc.\n\n✅ **GSD** — Stuck loop detection,\ncrash recovery, context size limits,\nplan validation (max 2 iterations)\n⚠️ **Kiro** — Hooks system for\npre/post task checks\n⚠️ **Spec Kit** — `/speckit.analyze`\nfor consistency validation\n❌ **OpenSpec** — No guardrails\n❌ **BMAD** — No runtime enforcement\n❌ **Taskmaster** — No guardrails\n\n*Note: claude-code-harness (not in\nthis 6) is the guardrail-first tool*","x":1420,"y":530,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc_row2_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":1020,"width":2500,"height":500,"color":"5","label":"Additional Cross-Cutting Capabilities"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc7","type":"text","text":"## CC7: Human Gates / Approval Points\n\nExplicit points where human reviews\nand approves before proceeding.\n\n✅ **GSD** — Interactive gating at\ndiscuss, plan approval, UAT\n✅ **Spec Kit** — Each /command is\na human-initiated gate\n✅ **Kiro** — Per-phase approval\n(requirements → design → tasks)\n✅ **BMAD** — PRD approval,\narchitecture sign-off, story approval\n✅ **OpenSpec** — Proposal review\nbefore apply\n⚠️ **Taskmaster** — Task approval\n(but less structured gates)","x":-580,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc8","type":"text","text":"## CC8: UI/UX Design Support\n\nDedicated capabilities for frontend\ndesign, visual auditing, accessibility.\n\n✅ **GSD** — `/gsd:ui-phase` generates\nUI-SPEC.md design contract;\n`/gsd:ui-review` 6-pillar visual audit\n(layout, color, typography, spacing,\nresponsiveness, accessibility)\n✅ **BMAD** — UX Designer agent\nfor interface design, user flows,\naccessibility considerations\n❌ **OpenSpec** — No UI support\n❌ **Spec Kit** — No UI support\n❌ **Kiro** — No UI support\n❌ **Taskmaster** — No UI support\n\n*Major gap: only 2 of 6 frameworks\naddress frontend-specific concerns*","x":-180,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc9","type":"text","text":"## CC9: Cost / Token Tracking\n\nMonitoring and optimizing AI usage\ncosts across the development cycle.\n\n✅ **GSD** — Built-in cost and\ntoken tracking\n⚠️ **Taskmaster** — Progressive\ntool disclosure reduces token usage\n(all: ~21K, standard: ~10K, core: ~5K)\nbut no explicit cost tracking\n❌ **OpenSpec** — No tracking\n❌ **Spec Kit** — No tracking\n❌ **Kiro** — No tracking\n❌ **BMAD** — No tracking\n\n*Only GSD actively tracks costs.\nTaskmaster manages token budgets\nvia tool loading tiers.*","x":220,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc10","type":"text","text":"## CC10: Pause / Resume / Handoff\n\nPersisting state for context transfer\nacross sessions, teams, or breaks.\n\n✅ **GSD** — `/gsd:pause-work`\n(context handoff), `/gsd:resume-work`\n(full context restoration),\nSTATE.md tracks decisions + position\n⚠️ **OpenSpec** — `/opsx:continue`\nresumes work on a change\n⚠️ **Taskmaster** — Long-term context\nmaintenance across sessions\n❌ **Spec Kit** — No session mgmt\n❌ **Kiro** — IDE session only\n❌ **BMAD** — No explicit support\n\n*Critical for long-running projects\nwhere developers switch contexts*","x":620,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc11","type":"text","text":"## CC11: Composability / Layering\n\nAbility to combine with other frameworks\nor extend with external rules/plugins.\n\n✅ **OpenSpec** — Purely spec layer,\nexplicitly composable with execution\ntools (GSD, Superpowers)\n✅ **Taskmaster** — `task-master rules add`\nimports external frameworks,\nlayerable by design\n⚠️ **Spec Kit** — Agent-agnostic,\nworks alongside other tools\n⚠️ **GSD** — Self-contained but\ncan coexist with spec tools\n❌ **Kiro** — Closed IDE ecosystem\n❌ **BMAD** — Self-contained system\n\n*OpenSpec + Taskmaster are the most\nexplicitly composable tools*","x":1020,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"sdd_cc12","type":"text","text":"## CC12: Autonomous Operation\n\nAbility to run multiple stages without\nhuman intervention.\n\n✅ **GSD** — `/gsd:autonomous` runs\nall remaining phases unattended;\nmilestone-level autonomy;\nstuck loop detection + crash recovery\n⚠️ **BMAD** — Dev agent works from\nself-contained stories (medium autonomy)\n⚠️ **Kiro** — Can run all tasks\nin sequence\n⚠️ **Spec Kit** — `/speckit.implement`\nexecutes all tasks\n❌ **OpenSpec** — Step-by-step only\n❌ **Taskmaster** — Manual navigation\n(\"what's next?\" driven)\n\n*Only GSD provides true milestone-level\nautonomous operation with recovery*","x":1420,"y":1070,"width":380,"height":380,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_matrix_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":1580,"width":2500,"height":580,"color":"2","label":"Coverage Matrix — Framework × Ontology Stage/Capability"},
		{"id":"sdd_matrix","type":"text","text":"## Pipeline Stage Coverage\n\n```\n                    S1    S2    S3    S4    S5    S6    S7    S8    S9    S10\n                    Init  Gov   Req   Disc  Road  Arch  Task  Exec  Verify Compl\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nGSD                 ✅    ⚠️    ✅    ✅    ✅    ⚠️    ✅    ✅    ✅     ✅\nOpenSpec            ✅    ❌    ✅    ❌    ❌    ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅     ✅\nSpec Kit            ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅    ❌    ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅     ❌\nKiro                ✅    ✅    ✅    ❌    ❌    ✅    ✅    ✅    ⚠️     ❌\nBMAD                ✅    ❌    ✅    ⚠️    ⚠️    ✅    ✅    ✅    ⚠️     ⚠️\nTaskmaster          ✅    ❌    ✅    ❌    ❌    ❌    ✅    ✅    ❌     ❌\n─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nCoverage            6/6   2/6   6/6   2.5/6 1.5/6 4.5/6 6/6   6/6   3.5/6 2.5/6\n```","x":-580,"y":1630,"width":1040,"height":340,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sdd_matrix2","type":"text","text":"## Cross-Cutting Capability Coverage\n\n```\n                    CC1   CC2   CC3   CC4   CC5   CC6\n                    Agent Ctx   Multi Git   Deps  Guard\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nGSD                 ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅\nOpenSpec            ❌    ❌    ✅    ✅    ❌    ❌\nSpec Kit            ❌    ❌    ✅    ✅    ❌    ⚠️\nKiro                ⚠️    ⚠️    ❌    ⚠️    ❌    ⚠️\nBMAD                ✅    ✅    ⚠️    ⚠️    ⚠️    ❌\nTaskmaster          ❌    ⚠️    ✅    ❌    ✅    ❌\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n\n                    CC7   CC8   CC9   CC10  CC11  CC12\n                    Human UI/UX Cost  Pause Comp  Auto\n───────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nGSD                 ✅    ✅    ✅    ✅    ⚠️    ✅\nOpenSpec            ✅    ❌    ❌    ⚠️    ✅    ❌\nSpec Kit            ✅    ❌    ❌    ❌    ⚠️    ⚠️\nKiro                ✅    ❌    ❌    ❌    ❌    ⚠️\nBMAD                ✅    ✅    ❌    ❌    ❌    ⚠️\nTaskmaster          ⚠️    ❌    ⚠️    ⚠️    ✅    ❌\n```","x":480,"y":1630,"width":700,"height":340,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sdd_matrix_legend","type":"text","text":"**Legend:** ✅ = Full coverage  ⚠️ = Partial / implicit  ❌ = Not covered","x":1200,"y":1630,"width":680,"height":40,"color":"5"},
		{"id":"sdd_matrix_scores","type":"text","text":"## Framework Completeness Scores\n\n(✅=1, ⚠️=0.5, ❌=0 across 22 dimensions)\n\n| Framework | Pipeline (10) | Cross-Cut (12) | Total (22) | % |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| **GSD** | 9.0 | 11.0 | **20.0** | **91%** |\n| **BMAD** | 7.0 | 6.0 | **13.0** | **59%** |\n| **Spec Kit** | 7.5 | 4.5 | **12.0** | **55%** |\n| **OpenSpec** | 6.5 | 4.0 | **10.5** | **48%** |\n| **Kiro** | 6.5 | 4.0 | **10.5** | **48%** |\n| **Taskmaster** | 4.5 | 5.0 | **9.5** | **43%** |\n\n*GSD is the only framework exceeding 90% coverage.*\n*Spec-first tools cluster around 48-55% — by design,*\n*they deliberately exclude execution concerns.*","x":1200,"y":1690,"width":680,"height":280,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_group","type":"group","x":-600,"y":2220,"width":2500,"height":340,"color":"1","label":"Five Philosophical Stances — Each Covers Different Ontology Regions"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_1","type":"text","text":"## Spec-First\n\n**OpenSpec · Spec Kit · Kiro**\n\nStrong: S2, S3, S6, S7\nWeak: S4, S5, S8, CC1, CC2\n\n\"Specifications are the primary\nartifact; code is their expression.\"\n\n*Deliberately minimal on execution,\ntrusting the AI agent to handle it\ngiven good specs.*","x":-580,"y":2270,"width":320,"height":260,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_2","type":"text","text":"## Execution-First\n\n**GSD**\n\nStrong: S4, S5, S7, S8, S9, S10,\nCC1-CC6, CC9, CC10, CC12\nWeak: S2, S6 (embedded)\n\n\"Methodology and workflow discipline\ndrive quality; the harness does\nthe heavy lifting.\"\n\n*Covers the most ontology surface\narea of any single framework.*","x":-240,"y":2270,"width":320,"height":260,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_3","type":"text","text":"## Role-First\n\n**BMAD**\n\nStrong: S3, S6, S7, S8, CC1, CC8\nWeak: S4, S5, S9, S10\n\n\"Specialized AI personas mirror\nhuman team roles; quality comes\nfrom separation of concerns.\"\n\n*Strongest on planning intelligence;\nweaker on runtime execution and\nverification automation.*","x":100,"y":2270,"width":320,"height":260,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_4","type":"text","text":"## Task-First\n\n**Taskmaster AI**\n\nStrong: S7, CC3, CC5, CC11\nWeak: S8, CC9, CC10\nAbsent: S2, S4, S5, S6, S9, S10\n\n\"Decomposition and dependency\nmanagement keep agents on track;\nquality comes from granularity.\"\n\n*Narrowest scope but deepest in\ntask decomposition + dependency\nmanagement. Most composable.*","x":440,"y":2270,"width":320,"height":260,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_5","type":"text","text":"## Guardrail-First\n\n**(claude-code-harness — reference)**\n\nStrong: CC6, S8, S9\nWeak: S3, S7\n\n\"Runtime enforcement prevents\nbad outcomes; the harness\nconstrains rather than guides.\"\n\n*Not one of the 6 frameworks but\nincluded as the ontology demands\na guardrail-centric archetype.*","x":780,"y":2270,"width":320,"height":260,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"sdd_phil_insight","type":"text","text":"## Composability Thesis\n\nNo single framework covers all 22 dimensions at ✅.\nThe ontology suggests natural layering:\n\n**Spec Layer** (OpenSpec or Spec Kit) → S2, S3, S6\n**Execution Layer** (GSD) → S4, S5, S7, S8, CC1-CC6\n**Task Layer** (Taskmaster) → CC5, CC3, CC11\n**Verification Layer** → S9, CC6\n\nGSD comes closest to a monolith at 91%,\nbut even it is weak on S2 (constitution)\nand S6 (standalone design docs).\n\n⚠️ **No documented attempts at layering exist.**","x":1120,"y":2270,"width":760,"height":260,"color":"5"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"sdd_e_title","fromNode":"sdd_title","fromSide":"bottom","toNode":"sdd_pipeline_group","toSide":"top"},
		{"id":"sdd_e_s1_s2","fromNode":"sdd_s1","fromSide":"right","toNode":"sdd_s2","toSide":"left","label":"→"},
